From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:33:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/ane: initialise the unused scratch binding in the
 add-128 slots test

program_add128_slots_test() declares its scratch binding without an
initialiser, passes NULL instead of it to ane_h16_process_bindings(),
and then expects scratch.index == 0. That reads an uninitialised stack
variable. With CONFIG_INIT_STACK_NONE (the linux-aurora recipe config)
the test passes or fails by chance; under qemu it failed with "Expected
scratch.index == 0, but scratch.index == 0 (0x0)", the mark of an
undefined read. program_h17_sections_test() already initialises its
scratch binding the same way.

Fixes: da30e7795701 ("accel/ane: run linked H16 programs and load them one after another")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c
index 48c64c73a1..905ee53029 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c
@@ -562,7 +562,7 @@ static void expect_empty(struct kunit *test, const u8 *load, unsigned int slot)
 static void program_add128_slots_test(struct kunit *test)
 {
 	static const u32 direction[3] = { 1, 2, 1 };
-	struct ane_h16_process_binding bindings[ANE_H16_SURFACES], scratch;
+	struct ane_h16_process_binding bindings[ANE_H16_SURFACES], scratch = {};
 	struct ane_h16_load_slot slots[ANE_H16_LOAD_SLOTS];
 	struct ane_h16_load_layout layout = {};
 	struct ane_h16_load_plan *plan = kunit_kzalloc(test, sizeof(*plan), GFP_KERNEL);
